        -:    5:**
        -:    6:** Shift-and-permute fuzz of the cage count. For every frame of every
        -:    7:** LAMMPS dump in a directory, the hexagonal and double-diamond cage counts
        -:    8:** are compared with the unshifted frame under
        -:    9:**
        -:   10:**   - every half-box translation (each axis 0 or 1/2),
        -:   11:**   - N random translations, rewrapped into the box,
        -:   12:**   - N random permutations of the atoms.
        -:   13:**
        -:   14:** A translation keeps atom indices, so the cage set must match, not only
        -:   15:** the count. A permutation changes the atom-index key that selects one
        -:   16:** maximum packing among several, so the count must match and the
        -:   17:** particular cages may differ.
        -:   18:**
        -:   19:**   fuzz_cage_invariance TRAJ_DIR [trials]
        -:   20:**
        -:   21:** Exits 0 when every frame agrees, 1 on a mismatch, 2 when TRAJ_DIR
        -:   22:** cannot be read.
        -:   23:*/
